prep time: 10 minutes
---

Heat @olive oil{2½%tbsp} in a large #skillet{} over medium heat. Once the oil is shimmering, add @garlic{4-5%cloves}(minced), @oregano{¾%tsp} and @crushed red pepper{½%tsp}. Sauté for ~{1%minute} until garlic is light golden brown.

Add the @orzo pasta{1½%cups}(uncooked) and stir to coat well. Cook for ~{1-2%minutes} to lightly toast the orzo and incorporate flavors. Move around occasionally to prevent sticking.

Pour in @dry white wine{½%cup} and cook until the liquid mostly cooks down, about ~{1-2%minutes}.

Now add @diced tomatoes{14.5%oz}(canned, with juices) and simmer for ~{2-3%minutes}.

Add @vegetable broth{2½%cups}(low sodium) and @salt{½%tsp}(more to taste). Turn heat up to get it boiling. Once boiling, turn heat down to maintain a low simmer. Cover and cook for ~{7-10%minutes} or until liquid has mostly cooked down and orzo is tender. Stir often to prevent sticking and uncover the last few minutes of cook time.

Remove from heat and add @capers{3%tbsp} and @basil{1/2%cup}(chopped, sub with parsley). Stir to combine. Taste for seasoning and add more if needed. Let the orzo sit uncovered for ~{1-2%minutes}. This will give it time to thicken up. Serve with vegan parmesan and fresh-cracked pepper. Enjoy!